{
  "sn2.23:0.1": "Linked Discourses 2.23 ",
  "sn2.23:0.2": "3. Various Sectarians ",
  "sn2.23:0.3": "With Serī ",
  "sn2.23:1.1": "Standing to one side, the godling Serī addressed the Buddha in verse: ",
  "sn2.23:2.1": "“Both gods and humans ",
  "sn2.23:2.2": "enjoy their food. ",
  "sn2.23:2.3": "So what’s the name of the spirit ",
  "sn2.23:2.4": "who doesn’t like food?” ",
  "sn2.23:3.1": "“Those who give with faith ",
  "sn2.23:3.2": "and a clear and confident heart, ",
  "sn2.23:3.3": "partake of food ",
  "sn2.23:3.4": "in this world and the next. ",
  "sn2.23:4.1": "So you should dispel stinginess, ",
  "sn2.23:4.2": "overcoming that stain, and give a gift. ",
  "sn2.23:4.3": "The good deeds of sentient beings ",
  "sn2.23:4.4": "support them in the next world.” ",
  "sn2.23:5.1": "“It’s incredible, sir, it’s amazing, ",
  "sn2.23:5.2": "how well said this was by the Buddha.” He repeated the Buddha’s verses, and said: ",
  "sn2.23:6.1": "",
  "sn2.23:6.2": "",
  "sn2.23:6.3": "",
  "sn2.23:6.4": "",
  "sn2.23:7.1": "",
  "sn2.23:7.2": "",
  "sn2.23:7.3": "",
  "sn2.23:7.4": "",
  "sn2.23:8.1": "“Once upon a time, sir, I was a king named Serī, a giver, a donor, who praised giving. ",
  "sn2.23:8.2": "I gave gifts at the four gates to ascetics and brahmins, to paupers, vagrants, supplicants, and beggars. ",
  "sn2.23:8.3": "Then the ladies of my harem approached me and said, ",
  "sn2.23:8.4": "‘Your Majesty gives gifts, but we don’t. ",
  "sn2.23:8.5": "Your Majesty, pl